const lcm = {"A2_lesson_1":["Using kein instead of nicht for verb negation: \"Ich komme nicht\" not \"Ich komme kein\".","Confusing mein/meine with possessive: \"Mein Bruder\" vs \"Meine Schwester\".","Forgetting verb-second position with time expressions: \"Heute gehe ich\" not \"Heute ich gehe\".","Using du instead of Sie in formal introductions.","Omitting articles: \"Ich habe Bruder\" should be \"Ich habe einen Bruder\"."],"A2_lesson_2":["Putting the verb at the end in Imperativ: \"Geh!\" not \"Du gehst!\".","Forgetting to put the modal verb in position 2: \"Ich kann schwimmen\" not \"Ich schwimmen kann\".","Confusing um...zu vs damit for purpose clauses.","Using Präteritum for spoken language where Perfekt is preferred in German: \"Ich habe gegessen\" vs \"Ich aß\"."],"A2_lesson_3":["Using the wrong auxiliary: \"Ich bin gefahren\" vs \"Ich habe gefahren\" (movement vs transitive).","Forgetting the ge- prefix for regular Partizip II: \"gemacht\" not \"macht\".","Putting the Partizip II before the auxiliary in main clauses.","Forgetting the -t suffix for regular verbs: \"gearbeitet\" not \"gearbeit\".","Confusing separable verbs: \"Ich habe eingekauft\" not \"Ich habe gekauft ein\"."],"A2_lesson_4":["Using wenn for past one-time events instead of als: \"Als ich in Berlin war\" not \"Wenn ich in Berlin war\".","Confusing als vs wie in comparisons: \"größer als\" not \"größer wie\".","Putting the conjugated verb at the end in wenn-sentences: \"Wenn ich Zeit habe\" not \"Wenn ich habe Zeit\".","Using comma incorrectly before und/oder in main clause series."],"A2_lesson_5":["Putting the verb before the subject in weil-clauses: \"weil ich krank bin\" not \"weil bin ich krank\".","Forgetting the comma before weil: not using a comma between main and subordinate clause.","Using weil when denn would be more appropriate in spoken German (denn takes main clause word order).","Confusing weil with obwohl: \"weil es regnet\" vs \"obwohl es regnet\"."],"A2_lesson_6":["Using direct word order in indirect questions: \"Ich weiß nicht, wo er wohnt\" not \"wo wohnt er\".","Forgetting the comma before the indirect question.","Confusing ob and wenn: \"Ich frage, ob du kommst\" not \"Ich frage, wenn du kommst\".","Using question word order in embedded clauses."],"A2_lesson_7":["Using the wrong adjective ending: \"ein guter Wein\" vs \"einen guten Wein\" (Nominativ vs Akkusativ).","Forgetting adjective endings altogether after certain articles.","Using strong endings after definite articles: \"der gute Wein\" not \"der guter Wein\".","Confusing endings after ein-words vs der-words."],"A2_lesson_8":["Using Infinitiv without zu after modals: \"Ich kann kommen\" not \"Ich kann zu kommen\".","Conjugating both modal and main verb: \"Er kann kommen\" not \"Er kann kommt\".","Confusing durfte (was allowed) with konnte (was able to).","Using Präsens forms for past events: \"Ich musste\" not \"Ich muss\"."],"A2_lesson_9":["Using main clause word order after dass: \"Ich weiß, dass er kommt\" not \"dass er kommt\".","Forgetting the comma before dass.","Using dass when a different conjunction is needed (e.g. weil or obwohl).","Writing das instead of dass (relative pronoun vs conjunction)."],"A2_lesson_10":["Confusing an/auf/in with Accusative (movement) vs Dative (location): \"Ich gehe in die Stadt\" vs \"Ich bin in der Stadt\".","Using wrong preposition for common locations: \"bei der Arbeit\" not \"an der Arbeit\".","Forgetting article contractions: \"im\" not \"in dem\", \"zur\" not \"zu der\".","Mixing up auf (on top of) vs an (at/on vertical)."],"A2_lesson_11":["Omitting the reflexive pronoun: \"Ich wasche mich\" not \"Ich wasche\".","Using the wrong reflexive pronoun for Dativ: \"Ich wasche mir die Hände\" not \"Ich wasche mich die Hände\".","Forgetting that some verbs require Dativ objects: \"Ich helfe dir\" not \"Ich helfe dich\".","Confusing sich setzen (to sit down) with sitzen (to be sitting)."],"A2_lesson_12":["Using du-form for Sie-imperativ: \"Gehen Sie!\" not \"Geh Sie!\".","Forgetting the -e ending for du-imperativ of some verbs: \"Warte!\" not \"Wart!\".","Using wrong word order in Imperativ with pronouns: \"Mach es!\" not \"Es mach!\".","Using modal verbs in Imperativ constructions incorrectly."],"A2_lesson_13":["Using Präsens instead of Präteritum for war/hatte: \"Ich war\" not \"Ich bin war\".","Confusing sein and haben as Präteritum auxiliaries.","Forgetting to use time expressions correctly: \"letzte Woche\" not \"die letzte Woche\".","Using Perfekt where Präteritum is expected in written narratives.","Mixing temporal prepositions: \"im Sommer\" vs \"am Montag\" vs \"um 8 Uhr\"."],"A2_lesson_14":["Using als instead of wie for equality: \"so groß wie\" not \"so groß als\".","Adding umlaut incorrectly: \"älter\" vs \"alterer\".","Forgetting the -er/-ste suffix: \"schneller\" not \"mehr schnell\".","Double comparative: \"mehr besser\" instead of simply \"besser\".","Confusing comparative of gut (besser) with mehr (more)."],"A2_lesson_15":["Word order with adverbs: time before place: \"Ich fahre morgen nach Berlin\" not \"nach Berlin morgen\".","Confusing und/aber/oder vs subordinating conjunctions (different word order).","Forgetting the verb stays in position 2 after conjunctions like aber, denn, und.","Putting the adverb in the wrong position: \"Morgen gehe ich\" vs \"Ich gehe morgen\"."],"A2_lesson_16":["Using Akkusativ instead of Dativ: \"Ich gebe dem Kind\" not \"Ich gebe das Kind\".","Forgetting Dativ article changes: dem, der, den (plural).","Using wrong Dativ possessive: \"meinem\" vs \"meinen\" (Dativ vs Akkusativ).","Confusing Dativ and Akkusativ after certain prepositions.","Using mir/mich incorrectly: \"Das gehört mir\" not \"Das gehört mich\"."],"A2_lesson_17":["Using the wrong reflexive pronoun for body parts: \"Ich putze mir die Zähne\" not \"Ich putze mich die Zähne\".","Forgetting the definite article for body parts: \"Die Haare\" not \"Meine Haare\" when reflexive.","Omitting reflexive pronoun: \"Ich fühle mich krank\" not \"Ich fühle krank\".","Confusing anziehen (to dress) vs ausziehen (to undress)."],"A2_lesson_18":["Using wrong adjective endings in Dativ: \"mit einem roten Kleid\" not \"mit einem rotes Kleid\".","Forgetting adjective-noun gender agreement in clothing descriptions.","Comparative confusion with clothing sizes: \"größer\" not \"mehr groß\".","Using the wrong preposition for clothing: \"im Anzug\" vs \"in einem Anzug\"."],"A2_lesson_19":["Using von instead of Genitiv: \"das Buch von meinem Vater\" is acceptable but \"das Buch meines Vaters\" is more formal.","Forgetting the -s/-es ending on masculine/neuter nouns: \"des Vaters\" not \"des Vater\".","Confusing Genitiv articles: \"des\" (m/n), \"der\" (f/pl).","Omitting Genitiv in formal written German where expected."],"A2_lesson_20":["Using direct question word order in indirect questions: \"Ich frage, ob...\" not \"ob...\".","Forgetting to use subjunctive for polite questions: \"Könnten Sie\" vs \"Können Sie\".","Using wrong relative pronouns for technology contexts.","Confusing Nebensätze with Hauptsätze word order after dass, ob, w-words."],"A2_lesson_21":["Using wenn for past habitual actions that no longer occur: use früher + Präteritum instead.","Confusing comparative/superlative of monosyllabic vs multi-syllabic adjectives.","Forgetting als in comparisons: \"schneller als\" not \"schneller wie\".","Using the wrong umlaut in comparative: \"jung, jünger\" not \"jung, junger\"."],"A2_lesson_22":["Forgetting the reflexive pronoun with emotional verbs: \"Ich freue mich\" not \"Ich freue\".","Using haben instead of sein for certain emotional states: \"Mir ist kalt\" not \"Ich habe kalt\".","Confusing sich fühlen with fühlen (transitive): \"Ich fühle mich gut\" vs \"Ich fühle den Schmerz\".","Using wrong preposition with emotional adjectives: \"Angst vor\" not \"Angst von\"."],"A2_lesson_23":["Confusing Dativpräpositionen (aus, bei, mit, nach, seit, von, zu) with Wechselpräpositionen.","Using wrong case after Dativpräpositionen: always Dativ, never change.","Forgetting contractions: \"zum\" not \"zu dem\", \"zur\" not \"zu der\".","Mixing up nach (to a country/city) with zu (to a person/building) with in (into)."],"A2_lesson_24":["Mixed confusion from multiple A2 topics covered in this review.","Forgetting whether to use wenn, als, or wann in time clauses.","Word order errors with multiple conjunctions in complex sentences.","Using Perfekt where Präteritum would be more natural for written narratives about traditions."],"A2_lesson_25":["Mixed topic errors: cumulative mistakes from all A2 grammar areas.","Forgetting subjunctive for polite requests in B1 preparation: \"Ich würde gern...\"","Using simple sentences when more complex structures are expected at B1 level.","Omitting preparatory es in sentences: \"Es freut mich, dass...\" not \"Freut mich, dass...\"."]}
